# Tablekit — copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
# Nothing here is required for local development; every value has a working
# default. All of them matter in production.

# ── secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Signs staff session cookies and keys the IP hash in the rate-limit log.
# The app REFUSES TO START in production without this — a public default
# would mean anyone could mint themselves a staff session.
#   Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32
TABLEKIT_SECRET=

# ── storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the SQLite database lives. Relative paths resolve from the working
# directory. On a container, point this at a mounted volume — the default
# lives inside the image and is lost on every redeploy.
# TABLEKIT_DB_PATH=data/tablekit.db

# ── public URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The origin printed into QR codes. Set this in production: behind a proxy the
# request's own Host header can be an internal name, and a sticker printed
# with `http://10.0.0.4:3000` on it is scrap paper.
# TABLEKIT_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://order.roastandtoast.example

# ── seeding ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The owner account `npm run seed` creates. Change the password before the
# cafe goes live; the seed script prints whatever it used.
# TABLEKIT_OWNER_EMAIL=owner@roastandtoast.test
# TABLEKIT_OWNER_PASSWORD=
